There is two ways to get to the Trader in the standard game distribution.
One is two sectors due east of the startup location, while the other
is considerably harder to get to (down from the Large Cavern beyond the
Ghost Maze).  In the standard distribution, there is NO items in the trader's
to start with.  The trader can only sell what players sell to him/her.  How-
ever, a prudent game administrator will set the game up with a few items
in the trader's so that new players are not killed out of hand.  

To do this, edit the file "item.start" before starting the daemon for the
first time.  The first parameter for every item is the sector in which
the item lies.  Change the sector from [-3] (which is NONESUCH, or nowhere)
to [-4], which is the trader's for any item you wish to have the trader
offer initially.  If the game is already underway, you need to stop the daemon
(via mdg_stop), and the edit "item.start".  However, if you ever remove the
*.old and *.save files (effectively resetting the game to the start setup),
you will still need to edit the item.start file or your changes will be lost.

My setup is to put a sword, dagger, hide shield, and one each of plate, chain,
ring, scale, and leather armor up for sale, plus a couple of torches.  In
this fashion, those first few treasures (invariably Widgets and Doomahickies)
have some use other than just lugging about.

NOTE: Stuff in the trader's will eventually go away (DECAY_TRADER) after 4
days (game time) which is about 1.5 hours (real time).  Stuff you are 
carrying about decays and goes away after 9 days game time.  (So be sure
to use stuff up or drop and pick it up again on a frequent basis!)

I am currently working on a mod that will moves things from NONESUCH into
the trader's (DECAY_NONESUCH) that will keep the trader's stock "fresh" and
simulate a thriving business servicing "non-players" who are off adventuring
somewhere else.  I'll post the diffs when I am finished if anyone is interested.




